#: views/menu-settings.php:226
msgid "Table"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:230
msgid "Sections: options stacked vertically as a form — best for 5+ distinct choices. Table: compact grid — best for simpler products with fewer options."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:236
msgid "Hide Add to cart until all required options are selected"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:250
msgid "Hides the \"Add to cart\" button until every required option has a value. Reduces incomplete or incorrect orders — strongly recommended for print-on-demand products."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:256
msgid "Display product options on"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:262
msgid "Popup"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:266
msgid "Product Tab"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:270
msgid "Popup: options open in a modal overlay on top of the product image. Product Tab: options appear inline below the product description as a dedicated tab."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:276
msgid "Quantity button CSS selector"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:284
msgid "Advanced — only needed if your theme uses custom +/− quantity buttons. Enter their CSS selector (e.g. .qty-plus, .qty-minus) so volume pricing recalculates correctly when quantity changes."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:303
msgid "Hide selection summary"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:317
msgid "The summary panel shows buyers a recap of every option they selected before adding to cart. Keep visible to reduce confusion; hide for very simple, self-explanatory products."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:322
msgid "Float summary panel"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:336
msgid "When Yes, the summary sidebar scrolls with the buyer as they configure options — keeping their selections always visible. Recommended for products with long option forms."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:341
msgid "Hide swatch caption labels"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:355
msgid "Swatch buttons (colour/image squares) display a text caption underneath. Hide captions if your swatch images are self-explanatory — gives a cleaner, more visual layout."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:360
msgid "Tooltip position"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:364
msgid "Top"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:364
#: views/menu-settings.php:387
msgid "Right"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:364
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:364
msgid "Left"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:372
msgid "When an option has a \"?\" help icon, a tooltip appears on hover. Controls which side it pops out — pick based on your layout to avoid the tooltip being clipped off-screen."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:377
msgid "Dropdown sub-list direction"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:383
msgid "Below"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:391
msgid "For advanced dropdown fields with nested sub-options: \"Below\" opens the child list directly under the parent row; \"Right\" opens it as a side flyout. Choose based on your available page width."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:410
msgid "Hide volume pricing table"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:424
msgid "Volume pricing tables show tiered discounts (e.g. 10 pcs = $5 each, 50 pcs = $4 each) to motivate larger orders. Hide if you do not use quantity-based pricing on this store."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:429
msgid "Volume pricing table style"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:435
msgid "Quantity range"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:439
msgid "Quantity breaks"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:443
msgid "Quantity range: shows a span (e.g. \"10–49 units → $5 each\"). Quantity breaks: shows a minimum threshold (e.g. \"10+ units → $5 each\"). Both display the per-unit discounted price."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:448
msgid "Live-update displayed product price"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:462
msgid "Yes: the product's main price display updates live as buyers pick options — they always see the full total. No: only the add-on price shows separately below the base price."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:467
msgid "Hide zero-value option prices"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:481
msgid "When an option adds +$0.00, that line still appears in the price breakdown. Enable this to hide zero-value lines and keep the summary clean — especially useful when many options are included by default."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:500
msgid "Force \"Select options\" on product cards"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:514
msgid "Replaces \"Add to cart\" with \"Select options\" on shop/category listing pages for products that have required options. Prevents buyers from bypassing the option form directly from the grid view."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:519
msgid "Show option swatches on shop grid"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:533
msgid "Renders option swatches (colour/material pickers) directly on product cards in the shop grid. Buyers can pre-select variants before clicking through to the product page — improves engagement and conversion."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:552
msgid "AJAX add to cart"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:566
msgid "Adds to cart without a full page reload — faster, smoother buyer experience. Disable only if your theme or another plugin conflicts with the cart counter when using AJAX."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:571
msgid "Disable persistent cart storage"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:585
msgid "WooCommerce saves cart contents to the database for logged-in users. For products with hundreds of custom options, this cart data can grow very large. Enable to skip database storage and reduce load — recommended for complex print products."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:590
msgid "Show \"Clear cart\" button"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:604
msgid "Adds a one-click \"Clear cart\" button to the cart page so buyers can start fresh without removing items one by one. Especially helpful for print-on-demand stores where customers frequently rebuild their order from scratch."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:609
msgid "Hide option details in cart"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:623
msgid "By default, the cart shows each chosen option beneath the product name (e.g. \"Paper: Matte, Size: A4\"). Hide when option names are technical or internal and not meaningful to the buyer — keeps cart line items clean and readable."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:628
msgid "Hide option add-on prices in cart"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:642
msgid "Hides the per-option price breakdown in the cart (e.g. \"+$2.00 for Matte finish\" disappears). The line item total and order total still include all costs — only the individual add-on amounts are hidden. Useful when showing a breakdown could confuse buyers or reveal internal pricing logic."
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:647
msgid "Hide option add-on prices in orders &amp; emails"
msgstr ""

#: views/menu-settings.php:661
msgid "Hides per-option pricing from order confirmation pages, customer emails, and PDF invoices. The order total remains accurate — only the breakdown by option is hidden. Recommended for quote-based workflows or when add-on pricing is internal-only and should not appear on customer-facing documents."
msgstr ""

